        "source_file_sha": "501227a8f839924784544480edea83967f017a68",
        "lead_summary": "Banks don't sell off on lower oil; they sell off when loan losses are coming. Monday it was Moynihan's own mouth \u2014 a double-digit Q3 trading-revenue warning that took BAC down and every broker with it. Wednesday the Fed hiked 12-0. Thursday the whole complex fell 3.7\u20134% on credit-cycle anxiety as oil's collapse stopped reading as relief and started reading as demand destruction. XLF fell all five sessions to $55.86 (-2.4% W/W), through the 50D, through the $57.48 pivot, to close at the week's low. The curve bear-flattened to +26bp. The sector that was supposed to WIN the hike just priced the recession the hike might cause.",
